{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /local/home/scheschb/.codex/plugins/cache/aim/AmazonBuilderCoreAIAgents-core/1.0.6505391367/skills/brazil/references/build-and-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Build and Test\n\n## Build Systems by Language\n\nBrazil supports multiple language-specific build systems:\n\n| Language | Build System | Documentation |\n|----------|--------------|---------------|\n| Java/Kotlin | brazil-gradle | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/BrazilBuildSystem/BrazilGradle/ |\n| Java/Kotlin | happytrails/happiertrails | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/BrazilBuildSystem/HappyTrails/ |\n| TypeScript/JavaScript | npm-pretty-much | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/NpmPrettyMuch/GettingStarted/v1 |\n| Python | brazil-python | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/BrazilPython3/ |\n| Go | bgo-wrap-make | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/GoLang/BrazilMakeGo |\n| Rust | brazil-cargo | - |\n| C/C++ | brazil-cmake | https://code.amazon.com/packages/BrazilCMake |\n| Scala | brazil-sbt | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/Scala/BrazilSbt/ |\n| Scala | happiertrails | https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/Scala/Using |\n\n## Configuration\n\nConfigure build system in Config file:\n```\nbuild-system = brazil-gradle;\nbuild-tools = {\n    1.0 = {\n        JDK17 = 1.0;\n        BrazilGradle = 8.x;\n    };\n};\n```\n\n## Build Commands\n\n### Universal Commands\nEvery build system supports:\n```bash\n# Run full build with tests and checks (same as build fleet)\nbrazil-build release\n```\n\n### Common Commands\nMost build systems support:\n```bash\n# Standard build\nbrazil-build\n\n# Run tests\nbrazil-build test\n\n# Clean artifacts\nbrazil-build clean\n```\n\n### Language-Specific Commands\nCheck language-specific reference files for additional commands.\n\n## Build Output Management\n\nBuild output can be very verbose, potentially overwhelming context and degrading conversation quality. This is especially problematic during test-fix-rebuild cycles.\n\n### Recommended: Log File Redirection\n\n```bash\n# Run build and show only last 20 lines (most relevant for success/failure)\nbrazil-build release > build.log 2>&1 && echo -e \"\\n\\n=== BUILD SUMMARY (LAST 20 LINES) ===\\n\" && tail -n 20 build.log\n\n# Filter for specific patterns\nbrazil-build release > build.log 2>&1 && grep -A 5 \"ERROR\\|FAILED\\|PASSED\" build.log\n\n# Examine logs incrementally if build fails\ntail -n 50 build.log           # First 50 lines\ntail -n 100 build.log | head -n 50  # Next 50 lines\n```\n\n### Build Artifacts\n\nBrazil typically writes artifacts to `build/` directory under the package:\n```\nPackageName/\n├── src/\n├── build/  (symlink to actual build directory)\n│   ├── private/  (intermediate build files, not published)\n│   └── [published artifacts]\n└── Config\n```\n\n**Important:** Use `brazil-build clean` to reset package, not manual deletion of build/ contents.\n\n## Testing\n\n### Running Tests\n```bash\n# Run all tests\nbrazil-build test\n\n# Run specific test (language-specific, see language guides)\n# Example for HappierTrails:\nbrazil-build single-unit-test -DtestClass=my.package.MyClass\n```\n\n### Test Configuration\nConfigure test frameworks in your build system:\n- Java: JUnit, TestNG\n- JavaScript: Jest, Vitest\n- Python: pytest, unittest\n- Go: go test\n- Rust: cargo test\n\n### Test Dependencies\nAdd test-only dependencies in Config:\n```\ntest-dependencies = {\n    1.0 = {\n        JUnit5 = 5.x;\n        Mockito = 4.x;\n    };\n};\n```\n\n## Building Multiple Packages\n\n### From Package Directory\n```bash\ncd src/PackageName\nbrazil-build release\n```\n\n### From Workspace src/ Directory\n```bash\n# Build all packages in topological order\nbrazil-recursive-cmd -allPackages brazil-build release\n\n# Build specific packages\nbrazil-recursive-cmd -p Package1 -p Package2 brazil-build release\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Build Fails with \"Cannot Find Build Directory\"\n**Problem:** Running build from workspace root instead of package directory\n**Fix:** Navigate to package: `cd src/PackageName`\n\n### Build Fails After Adding Dependencies\n**Problem:** New dependencies not in version set\n**Fix:** Run `brazil workspace merge` to merge dependencies\n\n### Tests Fail Intermittently\n**Problem:** Test isolation issues or timing problems\n**Fix:**\n- Run tests multiple times to confirm\n- Check for shared state between tests\n- Review test setup/teardown\n\n### Build Succeeds Locally but Fails on Build Fleet\n**Problem:** Environment differences or missing dependencies\n**Fix:**\n- Ensure all dependencies in Config\n- Check build-tools versions match\n- Test with `brazil-build release` (same as build fleet)\n\n### Verbose Output Overwhelming\n**Problem:** Too much build output in conversation\n**Fix:** Redirect to log file and examine incrementally (see Build Output Management)\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always build before committing** - Verify changes don't break build\n2. **Use `brazil-build release`** - Runs same checks as build fleet\n3. **Clean before major changes** - `brazil-build clean` resets state\n4. **Redirect verbose output** - Use log files for large builds\n5. **Test thoroughly** - Run full test suite before CR\n6. **Check language-specific guides** - Each build system has unique features\n7. **Build from package directory** - Never from workspace root\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
